sion-capital-programme.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"10/02/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Cabinet Member Advisory Panel for Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND)","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Commission","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-04","committee":"Governance & Audit Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed; Extraordinary","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-11","committee":"Standing Advisory Council for Religious Education (SACRE)","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Commission","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-18","committee":"Governance & Audit Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-17","committee":"Appointment Committee Assistant Director:Finance","time":"9.00 am","status":"Cancelled","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-03","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Commission","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Governance & Audit Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democratic.bracknell-forest.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Pension liability increased significantly and is creating ongoing revenue pressure","lead":"Growing pension deficits create unpredictable revenue pressures and reduce the stability of financial forecasts that lenders rely on when assessing creditworthiness and repayment capacity.","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"Revenue outturn annexes","paper_url":"https://bracknell-forest.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s224259/224259.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Council is running down cash reserves while capital financing requirement grows, reducing borrowing headroom","lead":"A council that has depleted internal cash reserves to fund operations has reduced financial flexibility and approaching limits to internal financing capacity. Future capital needs or revenue pressures may force external borrowing at potentially unfavorable\u2026","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"Revenue outturn annexes","paper_url":"https://bracknell-forest.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s224259/224259.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Fleet and transport costs within education services significantly exceeded budget","lead":"Material operational overspends in core services suggest either service inefficiencies or unanticipated cost inflation that may recur in future years, affecting budget sustainability.","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"Revenue outturn annexes","paper_url":"https://bracknell-forest.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s224259/224259.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Revenue outturn annexes","paper_url":"https://bracknell-forest.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s224259/224259.pdf","headline":"Pension liability increased significantly and is creating ongoing revenue pressure","detail":"The council's share of the Royal County of Berkshire Pension Fund's deficit increased from \u00a349.015m in March 2025 to \u00a359.653m in March 2026, a \u00a310.638m deterioration. The outturn notes that additional pension deficit employers' contributions were required, primarily due to academizations. This volatile and growing liability creates ongoing revenue pressure.","category":"other","matters":"Growing pension deficits create unpredictable revenue pressures and reduce the stability of financial forecasts that lenders rely on when assessing creditworthiness and repayment capacity.","figures":"Pension liability March 2026: -\u00a359.653m; March 2025: -\u00a349.015m; Deterioration: \u00a310.638m; Additional contributions due to academizations: \u00a30.053m","quote":"additional pensions deficit employers' contributions primarily due to academisations","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Revenue outturn annexes","paper_url":"https://bracknell-forest.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s224259/224259.pdf","headline":"Council is running down cash reserves while capital financing requirement grows, reducing borrowing headroom","detail":"The council maintains an under-borrowed position: Capital Financing Requirement stands at \u00a3239.6m but actual borrowing is only \u00a3127.5m, with the gap bridged by using internal cash reserves. The CFR increased \u00a37.6m during 2025/26. The council explicitly states that 'internal funds have reduced' and that it 'became limited' in its ability to continue internal financing, forcing increased reliance on short-term borrowing at average rates of 4.40%.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A council that has depleted internal cash reserves to fund operations has reduced financial flexibility and approaching limits to internal financing capacity. Future capital needs or revenue pressures may force external borrowing at potentially unfavorable rates.","figures":"CFR March 2026: \u00a3239.629m (up from \u00a3232.004m); Actual borrowing: \u00a3127.500m; Net borrowing position: \u00a3115.971m; Short-term borrowing: \u00a367.5m at average 4.40%","quote":"However, the Council's ability to continue with such a strategy in 2025/26 became limited as internal funds have reduced and borrowing was required to fund the Council's capital investment programme in addition to ensuring sufficient short-term liquidity","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Revenue outturn annexes","paper_url":"https://bracknell-forest.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s224259/224259.pdf","headline":"Fleet and transport costs within education services significantly exceeded budget","detail":"Education and Learning reported a total overspend of \u00a31.025m, with \u00a30.737m coming from Fleet & Transport alone\u2014the single largest pressure within that \u00a31.025m. This is a material operational cost pressure in a core service area and was only partially offset by staffing underspends.","category":"overspend","matters":"Material operational overspends in core services suggest either service inefficiencies or unanticipated cost inflation that may recur in future years, affecting budget sustainability.","figures":"Fleet & Transport overspend: \u00a30.737m; Education & Learning total overspend: \u00a31.025m","quote":"There was an overspend within Fleet & Transport of \u00a30.737m which was partially offset by underspends within staffing (-\u00a30.075m) to create an overall pressure of \u00a30.662m","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Revenue outturn annexes","paper_url":"https://bracknell-forest.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s224259/224259.pdf","headline":"Leisure utility indemnification charges are material and include prior-year catch-up","detail":"Leisure services overspent by \u00a30.243m, driven almost entirely by utility indemnification charges of \u00a30.260m. This included \u00a30.019m relating to the prior year (2024/25), suggesting either a contractual obligation or contingent liability that extends beyond the current year.","category":"overspend","matters":"Material costs paid through indemnification rather than as direct charges may indicate an underlying contractual or liability issue that creates ongoing future revenue pressure.","figures":"Leisure overspend: \u00a30.243m; Utility Indemnification: \u00a30.260m; Current year: \u00a30.241m; Prior year catch-up: \u00a30.019m","quote":"The overspend within Leisure relates to the Utility Indemnification charges applicable across the sites, this totals \u00a30.260m and includes \u00a30.241m relating to 25/26 plus an additional \u00a30.019m relating to 24/25","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Revenue outturn annexes","paper_url":"https://bracknell-forest.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s224259/224259.pdf","headline":"Building Control is a chronic loss-making service with no path to cost recovery","detail":"Building Control income has declined every year since 2016/17 and has never achieved the level needed to cover its costs. The 2025/26 outturn shows \u00a30.230m overspend: income underachieved by \u00a30.112m and agency staffing costs overran by \u00a30.142m. The council explicitly states that external competition makes it unlikely this service will ever break even.","category":"overspend","matters":"A service losing money for a decade with no realistic recovery plan represents an ongoing structural drain that reduces resources available for debt service and general fund resilience.","figures":"Building Control overspend: \u00a30.230m; Income shortfall: \u00a30.112m; Agency staffing overspend: \u00a30.142m; Income decline ongoing since 2016/17","quote":"Building Control income budget is set to reflect it should cover cash expenditure and non-cash budgets. Actual income has been in decline since 2016/17 and service has never achieved the necessary income level to offset deficits on account. External, non-local authority competition makes is unlikely income will ever offset costs.","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-09"},"name":"Bracknell Forest UA","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Pension liability increased significantly and is creating ongoing revenue pressure","lead":"Growing pension deficits create unpredictable revenue pressures and reduce the stability of financial forecasts that lenders rely on when assessing creditworthiness and repayment capacity.","also":["6 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Cabinet on 2026-10-13","n_findings":7,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Revenue outturn annexes","top_paper_url":"https://bracknell-forest.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s224259/224259.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":59,"news_drafts_total":3}}